No data from the cartridge
--------------------------

The repository contains no data blocks taken from Konami's game: no ROM image,
no asset pack, no tiles, maps, music or sound-effect captures, no screenshots
and no oracle fixtures. Small constants and rule tables that describe the
game's behaviour, such as those in `crates/gradius-core/src/stage1_tables/` and
`stage1_enemies.rs`, are functional values, not cartridge data. `scripts/check-rom-data.sh` runs in
`scripts/verify` and in CI and fails on a tracked file that looks like extracted
data.

Those files are generated on your own machine from your own Gradius (E)
cartridge, with `GRADIUS_ROM=<rom> scripts/extract-data`: `assets/gradius.pak`,
the copy staged for the web demo (`web/gradius.pak`) and `tests/fixtures/*`
(except the input `.script` files, which are this project's). They are derived
from Konami's work, remain Konami's copyright, and are not covered by the
project's MIT/Apache-2.0 grant. Use them only for your own play, research and
testing. Do not redistribute them, or any build that embeds them.

The published downloads (the Linux AppImage and the Windows zip) and the web
build contain no data from the cartridge either. On first start the game builds
`gradius.pak` from the ROM file the player gives it, on that player's own
machine. That pack is personal: do not upload it, share it or put it in a
release.

